diff --git a/docs/metadata-admission.md b/docs/metadata-admission.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..447083e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/metadata-admission.md
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# Registration and telemetry ping admission
+
+3 October 2026. The collector now projects the native efsn registration fields
+before storing or broadcasting them. Its credential ID supplies `name`; the
+reported name and unknown extensions are discarded. Required fields are:
+
+- Nonempty strings: `node`, `net`, `protocol`, `api`, `os`, `os_v`, `client`.
+- Integer `port` from 0 through 65535, including the disabled listener value 0.
+- Boolean `canUpdateHistory`.
+
+The projected object, including the credential-derived name, must serialize to
+at most **2048 UTF-8 JSON bytes**. This counts property names, punctuation and
+escaping, not JavaScript string length. Unknown extensions do not consume this
+retained budget; the existing whole-message transport cap still bounds input.
+Invalid registration closes the session before reserving its identity or changing
+the collection. Existing credential, duplicate-session and rotation rules apply.
+
+Authenticated `node-ping.clientTime` must be a nonempty string whose serialized
+JSON value occupies at most **128 UTF-8 bytes**, including quotes and escapes.
+The accepted string is echoed unchanged. Invalid values close that session and
+are not echoed. Pings do not refresh block, stats or pending-report receipts.
+This preserves the native efsn `time.Now().String()` report without parsing its
+timezone or trusting it as a collector timestamp. Numeric/custom ping formats
+are outside this candidate interface.
+
+These are dashboard interface limits, not consensus or block-size rules. The
+production change is confined to `server.js`, `lib/telemetry-info.js` and the
+ping case in `lib/telemetry-report.js`. Current-head transactions, history,
+snapshot storage, frontend, dependencies and efsn are unchanged.
+
+The 2 KiB bound excludes the IP subsequently attached by `Node.setGeo`. Primus
+derives that address from its connection/forwarding middleware; it is not proof
+of the original remote peer. Its inherited `forwarded-for` dependency accepts
+several proxy header names. The final proxy must normalize/remove untrusted
+forwarding headers, and the address must be included in aggregate size review.
+This change alone does not establish a maximum complete inventory.
+
+Validation: five new regression cases fail on the previous source; the candidate
+passes 167 contracts and 13 real loopback socket tests. Boundaries include UTF-8,
+JSON escapes, exact-size acceptance, one-byte overflow, metadata projection,
+session replacement and unchanged report receipts. The output-queue test now
+uses multiple bounded ordinary pings instead of a single 3000-character echo.
+
+An actual synthetic efsn node passes through collector, PostgreSQL, HTTP API and
+the unchanged compiled browser. Native metadata measures 201 bytes; timestamp
+values 57–58 bytes. Current-head hashes and fifty historical blocks match direct
+RPC, and all four browser checkpoints pass, including writer stop/expiry/recovery.
+No real wallet, backup or public endpoint is involved.
+
+The first two integration attempts reached the browser checkpoints but failed
+the zero-writer-error assertion. Added diagnostics locate two `ECONNREFUSED`
+errors before Windows could reach the already-listening WSL port. The fixture
+now performs a bounded Windows TCP readiness check and stops the writer before
+the server during cleanup. Final run: four refused readiness probes, a successful
+probe after 441 ms, then zero writer errors and normal closure on stop. Production
+retry behavior, deadlines and byte limits were not changed. Failed attempts are
+retained; this does not resolve the separately recorded older freshness failure.
+
+Evidence is retained in the node repository at
+`docs/evidence/restart-dashboard-admission-2026-10-03/`.
+Next: bound complete heads and their extensions while preserving required hashes;
+coordinate the credential roster, inactive rows and snapshot/output budgets.
+The eight-reporter 4/1/1 MiB profile remains measured test evidence rather than
+deployment defaults. Proxy/TLS, runtime review and collector loss during mining
+remain open.
diff --git a/lib/telemetry-info.js b/lib/telemetry-info.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..88b823e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/telemetry-info.js
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+function projectTelemetryInfo(value, identity) {
+    if (value === null || typeof value !== 'object' || Array.isArray(value)) {
+        return null;
+    }
+    var fields = ['node', 'net', 'protocol', 'api', 'os', 'os_v', 'client'];
+    if (!fields.every(field => typeof value[field] === 'string' && value[field].length > 0)
+        || !Number.isInteger(value.port) || value.port < 0 || value.port > 65535
+        || typeof value.canUpdateHistory !== 'boolean') {
+        return null;
+    }
+    var info = { name: identity };
+    fields.forEach(function (field) {
+        info[field] = value[field];
+    });
+    info.port = value.port;
+    info.canUpdateHistory = value.canUpdateHistory;
+    return Buffer.byteLength(JSON.stringify(info), 'utf8') <= 2048 ? info : null;
+}
+
+module.exports = projectTelemetryInfo;
